# CMS site_configs writes

## Invariant

Admin CMS edits persist to `public.site_configs` (`config_key = storefront_cms`). The homepage reads that row via `GET /api/site-config/public`. Local Zustand is not canonical.

## Write path

- Browser **must not** `supabase.from('site_configs').upsert` (RLS blocks `anon`; legacy local admin has no JWT).
- Writes go through `PUT /api/admin/site-config` (`requireSupabaseAdminUser` + service role).
- Client: `lib/siteConfigClient.ts` → `upsertSiteConfigValue` → same-origin fetch with `credentials: 'same-origin'`.
- Autosave stays admin-only (`SiteConfigStoreAutosave` on `/admin` while logged in).
- On logout, `setSiteConfigCloudWritesAllowed(false)` cancels pending upserts so template remount / pagehide cannot POST with a dead session (no false “Save failed” on the login page).

## Payload shape

Store the unwrapped partialize object (not `{ state, version }`). Use `unwrapSiteConfigValue` / `parseSiteConfigWriteBody` from `lib/siteConfigWritePayload.ts` on read and write so string JSON and nested `{ state }` rows still work (homepage, shipping CMS, admin save).

## Login

CMS save requires a Supabase Auth session whose email is on `admin_email_registry`. Do not re-open anon INSERT policies. If save returns 401, tell the admin to sign in with their Supabase email (not `admin` / `selpic2024`).
